<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40512" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-bullĭo</span></b> ,
			īvi or ii, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i> (Appuleian).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to bubble up</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 233, 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to cause to bubble
			forth</i>, <i>to cast forth with a bubbling
			noise</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 170, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spiritum,</span>”
				<i>to breathe out</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1</span></i>
			, p. 108, 16.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
